  "control_definitions": {
    "states": "For each sensitizer calculate S1/S2 and T1/T2 at minimum, enlarging roots to establish state character and adjacent-state competition; report actual SOC, not atomic Z scaling.",
    "geometry": "For Cy2, freeze the six consecutive backbone dihedrals listed in Cy2_planar_control.json to 180 degrees (an explicitly imposed all-trans planar control), relax all other coordinates, and compare the density-matched states against the relaxed molecule. Release all constraints and classify the resulting endpoint. This is a benchmark intervention, not an asserted minimum.",
    "rubrene": "Independently optimize rubrene S0,T1,S1 with root following, and all three sensitizer T1 states; no Cy2 self-TTA substitution.",
    "relativity": "Repeat decisive Cy2 SOC with a justified basis/relativistic treatment sensitivity. A spin-free ECP needs a supported SOC operator, not an assumed scalar-only conversion."
  },
  "observable_definition": "Matched vertical gaps and SOC are evaluated at each S0 geometry. For energy transfer use consistent adiabatic excitation energies: delta_TTET=E_T1(rubrene)-E_T1(sensitizer); negative is energetically downhill. Rubrene annihilation balance=2E_T1(rubrene)-E_S1(rubrene); nonnegative is an energetic prerequisite. These are not rates or quantum yields.",
